    "explanation": "This ruling decides no one's money: it sends the case to a human reviewer because the evidence cannot measure the part of the trip in dispute. The $34.42 charged stays held rather than collected or refunded.\n\nThe only GPS trace in the case (EV-GPS-00110) has a single 428-second gap — 18:35:00 to 18:42:08 — between the Defu Flyover portal fix and the Kallang portal fix, a 6.90 km straight line across the KPE tunnel. That is more than four times POL-RD-07's 90-second limb, and coverage is 81.7%. The artifact is impaired for POLICY purposes, not merely for the schema pre-pass, at weight 0.39 with issue codes GPS_GAP and LOW_COVERAGE, and it is the only measurement of the disputed stretch.\n\nRead the way POL-RD-07(i) requires — the straight line between the bounding fixes, the reading most favourable to the driver — the trip is 21.20 km against a booked optimal of 18.40 km, an excess of 2.80 km or 15.2%, just under POL-RD-01's 20% gate. But the admissibility assessment on the same artifact records that a surface route between the same two portals would put the trip at 25.50 km, over the gate, and nothing in the bundle distinguishes the two readings. The excess this case turns on lies entirely inside the stretch the trace cannot measure, so the excess limb is undecided there and supports neither a refund that needs it to be over nor a NO_ACTION that needs it to be under.\n\nThat is exactly the situation POL-RD-07(iii) addresses: with the trace impaired under (a) to (c) and no independent corroboration, the claim is not sustained on the present record and the outcome is ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION, because the absence of proof is a data failure and not a finding for the driver. POL-RD-10(3) makes escalation mandatory on the same facts.\n\nNone of the independent sources POL-RD-07(ii) names is on file. The chat log (EV-CHAT-00110, weight 0.60, TRUNCATED_LOG; last message 18:26:14, 2,186 s before the trip ended) contains no driver admission of an off-optimal route — 'going KPE ah boss' describes the very corridor the platform's own optimal route uses. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00110, weight 0.75, PARTIAL_RECORD) carries erp_gantries null, so no charged gantry places the vehicle off the optimal corridor. The counterparty statement asserts the same KPE route and concedes nothing against the driver's interest. And trip_record.actual_distance_km (21.20) is, on its own admissibility note, derived from this trace, so it is not independent corroboration either.\n\nConfidence is capped at 0.39 by POL-GEN-02(2): the deciding fact — the length of the disputed stretch — is carried by the impaired trace alone and by no independent artifact. That is below the 0.70 platform floor, a further escalation trigger under POL-RD-10(1).\n\nOn the driver's central claim, that no deviation exists because the excess is under the gate: the driver-favourable straight-line reading is the one I have used and I accept it as the mandated reading, but it cannot close the case, for the reason above. On the rider's duration point: elapsed time enters this policy only through POL-RD-02, which runs only once a deviation is established, so the 39 minutes give no separate ground. On the $3.00 of ERP: erp_gantries carries no coordinates, so under POL-RD-09(4) the gantry match is undecidable, the line is treated as matched, it is not a phantom charge, and no billing-integrity referral arises. On the profiles: the driver has no repeat-deviation pattern (deviation_flags_90d 0 against 744 completed trips in the same window), so POL-RD-06 is not engaged and no conduct referral arises; the rider's deviation_claims_60d is 1, below POL-RD-08's threshold of 4, so no heightened corroboration applies. No referral-producing clause fires.\n\nWhat would resolve this, for the reviewer: an LTA traffic advisory covering the KPE or ECP in the 18:19–19:02 window on 22 July 2026 (the advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-00110-01, is missing at weight 0.0), a driver admission in the chat log, gantry itemisation in the fare breakdown placing the vehicle off the optimal corridor, or a distance figure derived independently of this trace."
  },
