    {
      "claim": "A deviation may not be established on the gps_trace alone and must be corroborated by one of the independent sources POL-RD-07(ii) names. None is present. There is no driver admission in the chat log: the driver's only message says he is going by the KPE, which is the corridor the platform's own optimal route uses - optimal_route_source reads 'optimal is KPE then ECP, crossing both gantries'. erp_gantries is null, so no charged gantry places the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route does not use. The counterparty statement asserts the same KPE route and admits nothing. And trip_record.actual_distance_km is, on the pre-pass's own assessment, derived from this very trace, so it is not independent corroboration. The chat log is itself impaired at weight 0.6 with issue TRUNCATED_LOG (last message 18:26:14, 2,186 s before the trip ended); I do not assert what was said after that point. Without an independent source the claimed refund cannot be ordered.",
